>> MF=12 PHOTON PRODUCTION MULTIPLICITIES AND TRANSITION          9222 1451  458
         PROBABILITIES                                            9222 1451  459
                                                                  9222 1451  460
MT=4: PHOTON MULTIPLICITIES FROM INELASTIC SCATTERING             9222 1451  461
 All data are carried over from ENDF/B-VI, as follows: Transition 9222 1451  462
probabilities are used for four discrete levels assuming 60% -    9222 1451  463
40% split.  Continuum added above 300 keV. Due to the fact that   9222 1451  464
only four levels are involved, the continuum probability is       9222 1451  465
large.  The multiplicities are zero above 1.09 MeV.               9222 1451  466
                                                                  9222 1451  467
MT=18: PHOTON MULTIPLICITIES FROM FISSION                         9222 1451  468
 All data are carried over from ENDF/B-VI. In that evaluation     9222 1451  469
photon multiplicities are taken from Hoffman and Hoffman (Ho74).  9222 1451  470
                                                                  9222 1451  471
MT=102: PHOTON MULTIPLICITIES FROM RADIATIVE CAPTURE              9222 1451  472
  The multiplicities for radiative capture from the               9222 1451  473
GNASH analysis are incorporated into the file.                    9222 1451  474
